{"path":"numeric/complex/casin","title":"casinf, casin, casinl","titleHtml":"casinf, casin, casinl","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/c/numeric/complex/casin","section":"numeric","kind":"page","summary":"If no errors occur, complex arc sine of z is returned, in the range of a strip unbounded along the imaginary axis and in the interval [−π/2; +π/2] along the real axis.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex\"><code>&lt;complex.h&gt;</code></a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-c99\" id=\"Version_1\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"kw4\">float</span> <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/complex\"><span class=\"kw743\">complex</span></a> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; casinf<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">float</span> <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/complex\"><span class=\"kw743\">complex</span></a> z <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (1) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(since C99)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-c99\" id=\"Version_2\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"kw4\">double</span> <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/complex\"><span class=\"kw743\">complex</span></a> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;casin<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">double</span> <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/complex\"><span class=\"kw743\">complex</span></a> z <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (2) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(since C99)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-c99\" id=\"Version_3\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"kw4\">long</span> <span class=\"kw4\">double</span> <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/complex\"><span class=\"kw743\">complex</span></a> casinl<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">long</span> <span class=\"kw4\">double</span> <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/complex\"><span class=\"kw743\">complex</span></a> z <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (3) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(since C99)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/tgmath\"><code>&lt;tgmath.h&gt;</code></a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-c99\" id=\"Version_4\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"co2\">#define asin( z )</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (4) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(since C99)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">1-3)</span> Computes the complex arc sine of <code>z</code> with branch cuts outside the interval <span class=\"texhtml\">[−1,+1]</span> along the real axis.</div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">4)</span> Type-generic macro: If <code>z</code> has type <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"kw4\">long</span> <span class=\"kw4\">double</span> <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/complex\"><span class=\"kw743\">complex</span></a></span></code>, <code>casinl</code> is called. if <code>z</code> has type <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"kw4\">double</span> <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/complex\"><span class=\"kw743\">complex</span></a></span></code>, <code>casin</code> is called, if <code>z</code> has type <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"kw4\">float</span> <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/complex\"><span class=\"kw743\">complex</span></a></span></code>, <code>casinf</code> is called. If <code>z</code> is real or integer, then the macro invokes the corresponding real function (<code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\">asinf</span></code>, <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/math/asin\"><span class=\"kw672\">asin</span></a></span></code>, <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\">asinl</span></code>). If <code>z</code> is imaginary, then the macro invokes the corresponding real version of the function <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/math/asinh\">asinh</a></span>, implementing the formula <span class=\"mjax-fallback texhtml\" data-tex=\"\\small \\arcsin({\\rm i}y) = {\\rm i}{\\rm arsinh}(y)\">arcsin(iy) = i arsinh(y)</span>, and the return type of the macro is imaginary.</div>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td>  z\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td>  complex argument\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>If no errors occur, complex arc sine of <code>z</code> is returned, in the range of a strip unbounded along the imaginary axis and in the interval <span class=\"texhtml\">[−π/2; +π/2]</span> along the real axis.\n</p><p>Errors and special cases are handled as if the operation is implemented by <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"sy2\">-</span>I <span class=\"sy2\">*</span> <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/casinh\"><span class=\"kw799\">casinh</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>I<span class=\"sy2\">*</span>z<span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>Inverse sine (or arc sine) is a multivalued function and requires a branch cut on the complex plane. The branch cut is conventionally placed at the line segments <span class=\"texhtml\">(-∞,-1)</span> and <span class=\"texhtml\">(1,∞)</span> of the real axis.\n</p><p>The mathematical definition of the principal value of arc sine is <span class=\"mjax-fallback texhtml\" data-tex=\"\\small \\arcsin z = -{\\rm i}\\ln({\\rm i}z+\\sqrt{1-z^2})\">arcsin z = -<i>i</i>ln(<i>i</i>z + <span class=\"t-mrad\"><span>√</span><span>1-z<span class=\"t-su\">2<br></span></span></span>)</span>\n</p>\nFor any z, <span class=\"mjax-fallback texhtml\" data-tex=\"\\small{ \\arcsin(z) = \\arccos(-z) - \\frac{\\pi}{2} }\">arcsin(z) = acos(-z) - <span class=\"t-mfrac\"><table><tr><td>π</td></tr><tr><td>2</td></tr></table></span></span>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"c\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;stdio.h&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;math.h&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;complex.h&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">void</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">double</span> <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/complex\"><span class=\"kw743\">complex</span></a> z <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> casin<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"nu0\">2</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/c/io/fprintf\"><span class=\"kw848\">printf</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"casin(-2+0i) =&nbsp;%f%+fi<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span>, <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/creal\"><span class=\"kw754\">creal</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>z<span class=\"br0\">)</span>, <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/cimag\"><span class=\"kw751\">cimag</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>z<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"kw4\">double</span> <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/complex\"><span class=\"kw743\">complex</span></a> z2 <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> casin<span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/conj\"><span class=\"kw760\">conj</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"nu0\">2</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"co1\">// or CMPLX(-2, -0.0)</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/c/io/fprintf\"><span class=\"kw848\">printf</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"casin(-2-0i) (the other side of the cut) =&nbsp;%f%+fi<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span>, <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/creal\"><span class=\"kw754\">creal</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>z2<span class=\"br0\">)</span>, <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/cimag\"><span class=\"kw751\">cimag</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>z2<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"co1\">// for any z, asin(z) = acos(-z) - pi/2</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">double</span> pi <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/math/acos\"><span class=\"kw673\">acos</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"nu0\">1</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">double</span> <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/complex\"><span class=\"kw743\">complex</span></a> z3 <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/csin\"><span class=\"kw790\">csin</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/cacos\"><span class=\"kw781\">cacos</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/conj\"><span class=\"kw760\">conj</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"nu0\">2</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy2\">-</span>pi<span class=\"sy2\">/</span><span class=\"nu0\">2</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/c/io/fprintf\"><span class=\"kw848\">printf</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"csin(cacos(-2-0i)-pi/2) =&nbsp;%f%+fi<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span>, <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/creal\"><span class=\"kw754\">creal</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>z3<span class=\"br0\">)</span>, <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/cimag\"><span class=\"kw751\">cimag</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>z3<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>casin(-2+0i) = -1.570796+1.316958i\ncasin(-2-0i) (the other side of the cut) = -1.570796-1.316958i\ncsin(cacos(-2-0i)-pi/2) = 2.000000+0.000000i</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"References\">References</h3>\n<div class=\"t-ref-std-11\">\n<ul><li> C11 standard (ISO/IEC 9899:2011): \n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 7.3.5.2 The casin functions (p: 190)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 7.25 Type-generic math &lt;tgmath.h&gt; (p: 373-375)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> G.7 Type-generic math &lt;tgmath.h&gt; (p: 545)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n<div class=\"t-ref-std-c99\">\n<ul><li> C99 standard (ISO/IEC 9899:1999): \n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 7.3.5.2 The casin functions (p: 172)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 7.22 Type-generic math &lt;tgmath.h&gt; (p: 335-337)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> G.7 Type-generic math &lt;tgmath.h&gt; (p: 480)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/cacos\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>cacos</span><span>cacosf</span><span>cacosl</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(C99)</span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(C99)</span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(C99)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>   computes the complex arc cosine <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/catan\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>catan</span><span>catanf</span><span>catanl</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(C99)</span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(C99)</span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(C99)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>   computes the complex arc tangent <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/csin\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>csin</span><span>csinf</span><span>csinl</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(C99)</span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(C99)</span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(C99)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>   computes the complex sine <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/math/asin\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>asin</span><span>asinf</span><span>asinl</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(C99)</span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(C99)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>   computes arc sine (<span class=\"mjax-fallback texhtml\" data-tex=\"{\\small\\arcsin{x} }\">arcsin(x)</span>)  <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td colspan=\"2\"> <div class=\"t-dsc-see\"><span><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex/asin\">C++ documentation</a></span> for <span class=\"t-dsc-see-tt\"><span>asin</span></span></div>\n</td></tr>\n</table></div>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"References","id":"References"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C reference"},{"path":"numeric","title":"Numerics"},{"path":"numeric/complex","title":"Complex number arithmetic"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"casinf, casin, casinl","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"4 declarations. Computes the complex arc sine of z with branch cuts outside the interval [−1,+1] along the real axis."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"z"},{"label":"Return value","note":"If no errors occur, complex arc sine of z is returned, in the range of a strip unbounded along the imaginary axis and in the interval [−π/2; +π/2] along the…"},{"label":"Notes","note":"Inverse sine (or arc sine) is a multivalued function and requires a branch cut on the complex plane."},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"cacos, cacosf, cacosl","note":"computes the complex arc cosine"},{"label":"catan, catanf, catanl","note":"computes the complex arc tangent"},{"label":"csin, csinf, csinl","note":"computes the complex sine"},{"label":"asin, asinf, asinl","note":"computes arc sine (arcsin(x))"}]}]},"standards":["C99"],"wordCount":419,"codeBlockCount":2}
